  "generated_text": "To find the number of multiples of 10 between 9 and 101, we need to identify the first and last multiples of 10 within this range.\n\n1. The first multiple of 10 greater than 9 is 10.\n2. The last multiple of 10 less than 101 is 100.\n\nNow, we count the number of multiples of 10 from 10 to 100. This can be done by finding the number of terms in the arithmetic sequence from 10 to 100 with a common difference of 10.\n\nThe first term $a_1 = 10$, the last term $a_n = 100$, and the common difference $d = 10$.\n\nUsing the formula for the nth term of an arithmetic sequence, $a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d$, we can find $n$:\n\\[ 100 = 10 + (n-1)10 \\]\n\\[ 90 = (n-1)10 \\]\n\\[ 9 = n-1 \\]\n\\[ n = \\boxed{10} \\]",
